  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44129720",
      "title": "Extracting User Input Values",
      "lectureOrder": 245,
      "videoOrder": 233,
      "sourceHash": "dc91d6193e506c7d13b03901e8e5ef0cd25e8533ff8a8bb15b031a01929273fc",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.3,
          "end": 2.1,
          "en": "So as we can see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 6.33,
          "en": "Angular does set up and manage quite a complex form object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.33,
          "end": 9.36,
          "en": "for our template driven form here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.36,
          "end": 11.52,
          "en": "And it does that all automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.52,
          "end": 14.76,
          "en": "because we in the end, only registered these inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.76,
          "end": 18.423,
          "en": "and did nothing else and Angular did all the heavy lifting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.38,
          "end": 22.56,
          "en": "Now, we can use this form object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.56,
          "end": 25.35,
          "en": "to extract the entered values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.35,
          "end": 29.19,
          "en": "with help of the value property here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.19,
          "end": 31.53,
          "en": "but we can also use it for validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.53,
          "end": 34.563,
          "en": "and for rejecting invalid values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.73,
          "end": 37.26,
          "en": "Now let's start by extracting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.26,
          "end": 40.44,
          "en": "the entered values first though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.44,
          "end": 45.187,
          "en": "I'll rename my parameter here to form data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.8,
          "end": 48.48,
          "en": "because as we can see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.48,
          "end": 52.5,
          "en": "there actually is a property named form in that object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.5,
          "end": 54.69,
          "en": "that is created by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.69,
          "end": 57.27,
          "en": "And I don't wanna write form.form here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.27,
          "end": 59.853,
          "en": "so that's why I renamed the parameter to formData.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.17,
          "end": 64.77,
          "en": "And then we can access this form object with .form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.77,
          "end": 68.553,
          "en": "And there, we can get hold of the values with .value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.66,
          "end": 73.11,
          "en": "And here we can then use .email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.11,
          "end": 75.18,
          "en": "to get hold of the entered email address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.18,
          "end": 78.60300000000001,
          "en": "or .password to get hold of the entered password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.09,
          "end": 85.92,
          "en": "So here, I could get my entered email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.92,
          "end": 87.34,
          "en": "by extracting it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.28999999999999,
          "end": 91.17,
          "en": "and of course, the entered password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.17,
          "end": 94.32300000000001,
          "en": "can be extracted like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.64,
          "end": 98.31,
          "en": "Alternatively, we could of course also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.31,
          "end": 100.2,
          "en": "still use two-way binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.2,
          "end": 102.24000000000001,
          "en": "Just to be very clear about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.24000000000001,
          "end": 104.72999999999999,
          "en": "We could still use two-way binding here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.72999999999999,
          "end": 108.93,
          "en": "and we would still get that Angular managed form object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.93,
          "end": 112.05,
          "en": "So if you prefer to get hold of the entered values with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.05,
          "end": 116.169,
          "en": "of two-way binding, you can absolutely still do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.169,
          "end": 119.4,
          "en": "But here, I don't want to use two-way binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.4,
          "end": 123.36,
          "en": "Instead I'll extract those entered values only when the form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.36,
          "end": 128.13,
          "en": "is submitted with help of this Angular created form object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.13,
          "end": 130.08,
          "en": "And therefore, now here we can of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.08,
          "end": 131.687,
          "en": "console.log(enteredEmail, enteredPassword);",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.25,
          "end": 135.123,
          "en": "like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 136.05,
          "end": 140.55,
          "en": "And if we do that, then hopefully, unsurprisingly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.55,
          "end": 144.66,
          "en": "if I enter some values here and I click log in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.66,
          "end": 146.433,
          "en": "they are being logged here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147.497,
          "end": 151.02,
          "en": "So that's how we can extract values with help of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 151.02,
          "end": 154.82999999999998,
          "en": "that form object that's created by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 154.82999999999998,
          "end": 158.82,
          "en": "Next, let's make sure that we also add some validation here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.82,
          "end": 162.15,
          "en": "and we make sure that invalid values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.15,
          "end": 164.043,
          "en": "can't be submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
